1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,838
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:15,473
<i>We Ardientes are the</i>
<i>rightful leaders of this town.</i>

3
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:19,352
<i>That is why we're going</i>
<i>to have Diego killed.</i>

4
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:22,230
[Raul] <i>Have our men guard Diego in jail.</i>

5
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:25,775
<i>I'm sure the Ardientes aren't happy</i>
<i>about the results of the survey.</i>

6
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:28,069
<i>If things get out of hand,</i>
<i>you know what to do.</i>

7
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:29,029
<i>Break Diego out.</i>

8
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:31,072
<i>Why don't you accompany me?</i>

9
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:33,783
[Ivy] <i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

10
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>Let's go home.</i>

11
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,954
[evil laugh]

12
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:40,457
<i>-Natalie?!</i>
<i>-In the flesh.</i>

13
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:44,002
<i>-What's your problem, Natalie?</i>
<i>-You murdered my poor father!</i>

14
00:00:44,085 --> 00:00:46,421
<i>It's payback time, Emilia!</i>

15
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:48,006
<i>Bad news, Congressman.</i>

16
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:51,342
<i>Jaguar's men broke into</i>
<i>the station and rescued Diego</i>

17
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,427
<i>from the hands of our men.</i>

18
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:55,680
<i>-We're Jaguar's men. Let's go!</i>
<i>-I don't care!</i>

19
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,140
<i>I'm not going with you!</i>

20
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:59,017
<i>You really are stubborn. Jaguar was right.</i>

21
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,685
<i>Wait! Who's Jaguar?!</i>

22
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:02,979
[Rufo] <i>Jaguar says you're</i>
<i>the one who needs him.</i>

23
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:05,190
<i>He will help you with your candidacy.</i>

24
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:08,651
<i>I'll defeat the Ardientes</i>
<i>using the force of the masses.</i>

25
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,820
<i>What I want is change for Ardiente,</i>

26
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:14,115
<i>not to replace one demon</i>
<i>with another demon.</i>

27
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,576
[Ivy] <i>I need to get out of here.</i>

28
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:18,369
<i>-Hello, Raul?</i>
<i>-Emilia?</i>

29
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:21,581
<i>Save me because Natalie</i>
<i>is going to kill me.</i>

30
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:22,749
<i>Save me now!</i>

31
00:01:22,832 --> 00:01:24,042
-[Natalie screaming]
-[gunshot]

32
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:28,379
<i>That bastard Jaguar is really</i>
<i>making my blood boil!</i>

33
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:29,631
<i>He's obviously challenging me!</i>

34
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:30,632
[Arnaldo] <i>Why? What happened?</i>

35
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:33,218
[Julio] <i>He kidnapped your mother and Ivy.</i>

36
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:34,719
<i>We need to save them.</i>

37
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:37,722
[Julio] <i>Jaguar is really getting</i>
<i>on my nerves.</i>

38
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,353
[screaming] [slapping]

39
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,314
Emilia! Emilia!

40
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:49,651
[crying]

41
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:54,030
Worst day of my life, Ivy!

42
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:58,076
This is the worst day of my life!

43
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,747
That Natalie…

44
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:05,542
This isn't over.

45
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:08,253
I will get back at that woman!

46
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:10,505
-Shh!
-The way she humiliated me…

47
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:12,173
[sobbing]

48
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:14,008
That's enough.

49
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,177
That's enough, Emilia.

50
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:20,056
You're Emilia Ardiente.
Crying doesn't suit you.

51
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:25,019
Emilia, if you're going
to have someone killed,

52
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:28,064
you should include their whole family.

53
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:32,485
And you should make sure they're all dead

54
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,195
so they won't take revenge on you.

55
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:37,866
Well, I understand Natalie

56
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:39,701
because if I were in her position,

57
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:42,412
flies would be swarming
all over you by now.

58
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:45,665
[ominous music playing]

59
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:49,168
Are you really my friend?
Whose side are you on?

60
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:55,508
You know, sometimes, I wonder if
you're really on my side, Ivy.

61
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:58,344
Because look at what you're doing.

62
00:02:58,803 --> 00:03:04,934
And I'm also wondering
about… about that Jaguar.

63
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,771
Why did he save me?

64
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,899
[ominous music continues]

65
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:14,277
Well, whatever his reason may
be, the important thing is…

66
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:18,615
Emilia Ardiente is still alive.

67
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:24,329
So, you have a chance to find
out who Jaguar really is.

68
00:03:24,787 --> 00:03:28,207
-[sobbing]
-[ominous music playing]

69
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:30,710
Raul?!

70
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:32,211
Natalie.

71
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:36,382
-What?
-What's your problem?

72
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:40,803
Why did you deny me of my prey?!

73
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:45,850
Natalie, it's not the right moment.
It isn't Emilia's time yet.

74
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:48,019
It isn't Emilia's time?

75
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,855
Or you can't live without her?

76
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:53,316
Let's admit it, Raul.

77
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:58,655
The truth is, you can't live
without your wife.

78
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:02,575
You feel so invincible.

79
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:05,203
You feel like an alpha male

80
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:07,121
because she boosts your ego.

81
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:09,707
She's so crazy about you.

82
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,169
No matter what you do to her,
no matter how many times

83
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,504
you cheat on her,

84
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:16,381
she's still there for you.

85
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:18,716
Wait, why are you saying this?

86
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,842
Admit it!

87
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:21,177
Are you jealous?

88
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,805
I'm irritated.

89
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,390
Irritated?

90
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:29,352
[tense music playing]

91
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:31,479
Natalie, listen.

92
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:34,983
All I need is for you to trust me.

93
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:38,111
Trust that you'll get what you want.

94
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:40,405
I trust you,

95
00:04:41,531 --> 00:04:44,701
but don't you dare break that.

96
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:49,372
Now, if you trust me,
you need to lie low for a while.

97
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,292
Natalie, you're in danger.

98
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:55,586
Especially now that Emilia knows
who she's up against.

99
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:58,715
She won't stop
until she knows you're dead.

100
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:00,675
Just wait a little more.

101
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:04,137
Wait until I've stripped
the Ardientes of their power,

102
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:06,556
then you can strike again.

103
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:07,932
I need to go.

104
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:10,101
Emilia's waiting for me.

105
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:12,562
[tense music continues]

106
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:15,815
Okay.

107
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:19,694
But you better think of a good excuse.

108
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:25,491
I might've said you were good in bed.

109
00:05:33,916 --> 00:05:35,793
Emilia, stop crying.

110
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,920
It doesn't suit you.

111
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:41,340
You'll really allow someone
like Natalie to get to you?

112
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:44,343
[crying]

113
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:46,179
Come here.

114
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,598
[crying]

115
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:52,393
[slapping]

116
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,479
I don't deserve this.

117
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:56,314
I don't deserve this!

118
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,608
I don't deserve this!

119
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:00,818
Do I deserve this? I don't, right?

120
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:04,822
Yes, you don't. You don't deserve this.

121
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:05,823
Of course not.

122
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,408
[crying]

123
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:08,701
Stop crying.

124
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,827
[crying]

125
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,704
It doesn't suit you, trust me.

126
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,290
And why won't this damn car start?!

127
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:15,833
Damn it!

128
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,710
[sobbing]

129
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,128
-[action music playing]
-[laughing]

130
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,130
-[crying]
-[laughing]

131
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:23,341
Sorry.

132
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,552
Sorry, Emilia. I'm sorry.

133
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:31,766
Sorry, I'll stop.

134
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:35,728
-You're mocking me again.
-No.

135
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:38,231
-You are!
-No…

136
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:39,732
Emilia.

137
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:41,484
-[honking]
-It's Arnaldo!

138
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:42,777
[Ivy] Hon!

139
00:06:43,694 --> 00:06:44,612
Hon!

140
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:45,571
[Emilia crying]

141
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:47,365
-Hon!
-Emilia!

142
00:06:47,698 --> 00:06:48,533
Hon!

143
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:49,784
-Emilia!
-[Ivy] Hon!

144
00:06:50,701 --> 00:06:51,702
Are you okay?

145
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:53,579
Are you hurt?

146
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,540
I'm okay. I'm fine.

147
00:06:55,623 --> 00:06:56,791
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

148
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,626
[somber music playing]

149
00:06:58,709 --> 00:06:59,961
How are you? Are you hurt?

150
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:01,129
[Arnaldo] How did you escape?

151
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:03,047
Ivy helped me escape.

152
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:07,593
That crazy ex of yours, Arnaldo…

153
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:10,888
How are you?

154
00:07:10,972 --> 00:07:14,517
Are you worried about me or Natalie?

155
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,477
[ominous music playing]

156
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:18,062
What?

157
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:19,605
Wait.

158
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,691
Why are you bringing Natalie up, Emilia?

159
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:26,070
Raul, she's your mistress!
You have a new mistress!

160
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:29,240
Emilia, listen. Stop saying that.

161
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:32,535
What does Natalie have to do with this?

162
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:37,248
I… Emilia, Natalie isn't
the kind of woman… Come on!

163
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:43,171
First of all Emilia,
she's your son's ex-girlfriend.

164
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:45,214
Why would I pursue her?

165
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,800
Why would I go for someone like her?

166
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,177
You know what?

167
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:51,929
That's why your father hates me!

168
00:07:52,388 --> 00:07:54,223
It's because of all your accusations!

169
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:55,641
And they're all false!

170
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:58,269
Emilia, I will never leave you for her.

171
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:01,939
If you only knew how worried
I was about you.

172
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:05,526
You can ask Arnaldo if you want, Emilia.

173
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,903
[crying]

174
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:08,488
Can you please stop being paranoid?!

175
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:09,780
[dramatic music playing]

176
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:12,575
Raul.

177
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:15,495
I'm here. Calm down.

178
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:29,509
And Ton says Jaguar has a huge net worth.

179
00:08:30,259 --> 00:08:32,512
If he's really working with Natalie.

180
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:36,182
That means Pablo had a lot of connections.

181
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,268
But it doesn't make sense.

182
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:43,147
If Jaguar really was our enemy,
why'd he let Emilia go?

183
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,690
[tense music playing]

184
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:49,820
To send a message
that we are at his mercy.

185
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:58,079
Damn. This Jaguar is really
getting on my nerves.

186
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:01,165
There's no point being upset with Jaguar.

187
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:04,377
Nothing bad happened to Ivy.
And he even let Emilia go.

188
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:06,003
Shouldn't you be grateful, instead?

189
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:07,505
[scoffs]

190
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:08,464
Grateful?!

191
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:13,553
I'd rather kill myself
than thank that bastard, Jaguar.

192
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:16,514
I should have killed him
when I got the chance.

193
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:19,976
I should have followed him
and shot him in the head,

194
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,143
so my problems would be over.

195
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:24,522
But now, I am going to
make him my project.

196
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:26,482
Because I will kill that man.

197
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:28,609
[tense music continues playing]

198
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:33,114
I won't allow Diego's accomplice

199
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:36,826
or some hotsie-patootsie
woman like Natalie

200
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:39,287
to ruin the name Ardiente.

201
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:49,755
Hon, just sleep here for tonight.

202
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:53,009
Come on. Natalie might come back for you.

203
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,510
I'll kill her if she tries.

204
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:59,015
Honey, relax. I'm okay now.

205
00:09:59,098 --> 00:10:03,311
And I'll have my bodyguards
with me, so I'll be okay.

206
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:05,938
Well, when it comes to your protection,

207
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,940
I don't trust anyone else but me.

208
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,775
So, please stay.

209
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:11,819
Come on.

210
00:10:11,902 --> 00:10:13,863
I can't relax knowing
you could be in danger.

211
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:16,657
Hon…

212
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:19,410
Please?

213
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:23,623
Okay.

214
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:25,791
Thank you.

215
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,545
Honey…

216
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:37,094
Your grandfather mentioned
Diego has a new ally.

217
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:38,054
[slow tense music playing]

218
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:40,389
Is he working with the Jaguar?

219
00:10:41,432 --> 00:10:43,434
[sighs] Well, yes.

220
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:47,897
We planned to have Diego killed,

221
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:50,399
but he managed to survive,

222
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:52,568
thanks to Jaguar's help.

223
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:56,614
And now he has constant
protection because of that.

224
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:01,202
Diego's really lucky, then.

225
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,287
He even found a new ally.

226
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:06,040
He's lucky to be alive, right?

227
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:07,416
Yeah…

228
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:11,087
which puts me
in a very difficult position.

229
00:11:12,546 --> 00:11:16,092
If they continue to work together,

230
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:17,718
I will lose the election.

231
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:21,013
I can't allow Diego to beat me.

232
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:23,724
Honey…

233
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,185
I don't see that happening.

234
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,021
Huh?

235
00:11:31,982 --> 00:11:35,027
I don't think Diego can beat you.

236
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:37,780
Of course.

237
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,951
He will never beat me,
knowing that I have you.

238
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:44,787
My secret weapon.

239
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:47,790
Of course.

240
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,794
[slow tense music playing]

241
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:58,217
[suspenseful music playing]

242
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:02,263
[Ivy] <i>The same weapon</i>
<i>that'll cut you down.</i>

243
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:08,936
[mobile phone ringing]

244
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:12,898
-Lily, finally!
-Mom.

245
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,608
I'm so glad you called.

246
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:16,235
How are you?

247
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:17,945
I'm fine.

248
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,029
But Diego…

249
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:21,699
<i>The Ardientes tried to get rid of him.</i>

250
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:23,826
Arnaldo tried to have him killed.

251
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:25,411
What?

252
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:26,245
[exhales sharply]

253
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:29,498
But he's okay, Mom. Someone helped him.

254
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:31,167
Who did?

255
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,626
It was the Jaguar.

256
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,295
<i>A leader of a syndicate</i>

257
00:12:34,712 --> 00:12:37,131
going against the Ardientes.

258
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:39,758
Lily, have a bad feeling
about this Jaguar.

259
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:41,802
Me too.

260
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:44,388
Even if he's going against the Ardientes,

261
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:47,308
Diego shouldn't trust him.

262
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:51,228
He really needs to be freed
from prison soon.

263
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:54,440
Okay, Lily. I'll take care of that.

264
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:57,860
I need to set my plans in motion, Mom.

265
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:01,071
Because the longer we wait,
the more complicated things get.

266
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:03,782
Just take care, okay?

267
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:07,077
I will, Mom. Mom, you take care too.

268
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:10,289
Let's just keep each other updated.

269
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,123
<i>Okay, then.</i>

270
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,084
Be careful, okay?

271
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,799
[tense music playing]

272
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:37,316
Ivy.

273
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:38,901
I won't stay long.

274
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:40,027
This is from Diego.

275
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,404
-Thank you.
-Okay.

276
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,000
[Diego] <i>Your plans need to push through.</i>

277
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:58,629
<i>Don't sacrifice seeking justice for me.</i>

278
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:02,550
<i>I can take care of myself.</i>
<i>I love you so much.</i>

279
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:05,261
[romantic guitar music playing]

280
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:12,768
Don't worry.

281
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:14,853
I can take care of myself.

282
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:18,440
Diego, your life is at stake.

283
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:23,112
What the Ardientes did to you
was against human rights!

284
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,072
[Georgina] Camia's right.

285
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:26,782
But don't worry.

286
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,577
The judge was already inhibited
from handling your case.

287
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,454
We're just waiting
to see who will replace her.

288
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:33,789
Then we'll file for an appeal.

289
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:34,999
Diego…

290
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,127
We already have enough evidence

291
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:39,837
to prove your innocence.

292
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:43,883
So, don't worry.
You'll get out of here soon.

293
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,634
[slow tense music playing]

294
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:46,760
[mobile phone ringing]

295
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,140
Hello?

296
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:52,766
Yes.

297
00:14:55,644 --> 00:14:56,604
Judge Otico.

298
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,065
Very well.

299
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:02,902
Then set a court appearance
as soon as possible.

300
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:04,403
Thank you.

301
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,531
So we have a new judge.

302
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:11,827
Let's just hope she isn't
a lapdog of the Ardientes.

303
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:18,667
Diego's lawyer already called me.

304
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:21,170
They asked me to set a court appearance.

305
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:24,465
Very good. Just stick
to the plan, Judge Otico.

306
00:15:24,548 --> 00:15:26,091
Understood, Jaguar.

307
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:29,303
All right, just wait for your bonus.

308
00:15:29,386 --> 00:15:31,430
You're really generous, Jaguar.

309
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:34,016
But remember, I'm a vicious enemy too.

310
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:37,102
[tense music playing]

311
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,939
Once I'm done helping Diego.

312
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:42,733
I'll deal with you, Emilia.

313
00:15:47,696 --> 00:15:48,656
Jaguar.

314
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:53,494
Have you sent the gifts?

315
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:54,745
Yes.

316
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:57,206
I'm sure she received it by now.

317
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:00,167
[suspenseful music playing]

318
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,711
Emilia, don't open it.

319
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:05,339
-Who knows? It's a bomb.
-[tense music playing]

320
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:08,050
Auntie, Jaguar told me to open it.

321
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:10,177
So, I should open it.

322
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:11,720
What if…

323
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:14,390
Natalie sent that?

324
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:17,977
Auntie, Jaguar saved my life.

325
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,688
So why would he kill me right away?

326
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:22,439
I'll open it.

327
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:26,527
[tense music continues]

328
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:29,029
Wow.

329
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:30,823
A cellphone.

330
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:37,663
I'll read it.

331
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:42,584
CALL ME, MY BEAUTIFUL.

332
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:43,502
[scoffs]

333
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:47,464
"Call me, my beautiful".

334
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:52,428
Jaguar's quite the sweet-talker, no?

335
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:54,763
Just like Raul?

336
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:57,808
Auntie, all men are like that.

337
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:01,395
I'll call him.

338
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,108
[tense music continues]

339
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:11,405
[mobile phone ringing]

340
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,077
Are you sure she won't recognize my voice?

341
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:18,370
She won't, Jaguar.

342
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,705
[mobile phone ringing]

343
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:23,876
Hello, Jaguar?

344
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:25,836
<i>Hello, beautiful.</i>

345
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:27,171
<i>Did I make your day?</i>

346
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,590
Can you just stop the flowery words?

347
00:17:29,673 --> 00:17:31,508
What exactly do you want from me?

348
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:33,802
It's simple.

349
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:35,929
<i>I want you.</i>

350
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:39,224
Well, if you really want me,
then show yourself.

351
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:41,727
You can't hide under your mask forever.

352
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:44,396
<i>Then let's meet.</i>

353
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:46,231
But I have one condition.

354
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:50,152
Condition? Okay. Tell me.

355
00:17:50,235 --> 00:17:51,737
<i>I want it to be just the two of us.</i>

356
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,238
No one else.

357
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:56,158
[tense music intensifies]

358
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,220
[tense music continues playing]

359
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,234
I'm ready for you, Jaguar.

360
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:31,902
I hope you are too.

361
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:33,904
[ominous piano music playing]

362
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,075
This is it.

363
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,121
Emilia.

364
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:43,497
Yes, Aunt Claire?

365
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,791
There's a limousine
waiting for you outside.

366
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,209
It's from Jaguar.

367
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:51,380
That man is full of surprises, Auntie.

368
00:18:52,756 --> 00:18:53,757
Take care, Emilia.

369
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:57,761
A man who is as clever and sly as him…

370
00:18:58,637 --> 00:19:00,013
can be the most dangerous predator.

371
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:01,598
Remember that.

372
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:03,600
Don't worry, Auntie.

373
00:19:04,309 --> 00:19:05,561
Remember this too.

374
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:10,649
A woman in red is fierce and smart enough

375
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:13,068
to make a sly man fall for her.

376
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:14,987
[ominous music playing]

377
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,364
I shall go now, Auntie.

378
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:24,872
[tense music playing]

379
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:30,544
Why?

380
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:33,922
Cut it out, Honey.

381
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:36,633
You've been like this all day.

382
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:42,306
-Well, I just…
-Wow, so clingy!

383
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:44,141
Your hands are all over the place.

384
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:47,102
I feel more comfortable
when you're close by.

385
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:51,356
You know, I'm just…I'm
just worried, that's all.

386
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:55,277
Worried? About what?

387
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:57,112
Well…

388
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:01,491
Honey, whatever you're worried about…

389
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,036
If it's about me, then don't be.

390
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,496
You should worry more about Diego.

391
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:09,333
Hon, do you think…

392
00:20:10,709 --> 00:20:12,544
our wedding's getting in the way?

393
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:16,340
Maybe we should focus
on your campaign more.

394
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:18,342
Remember, when it came
to the survey results…

395
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:19,593
[slow tense music playing]

396
00:20:19,676 --> 00:20:21,511
Diego had the upper hand.

397
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:23,180
No.

398
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:25,265
You're not getting in the way,

399
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:27,809
and neither is our wedding, okay?

400
00:20:28,518 --> 00:20:29,937
Don't ever think that.

401
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,439
The wedding will go as planned.

402
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,983
I don't care about those survey results.

403
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:37,945
The election's a long way off.
I can catch up.

404
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:41,657
What's important now is our marriage.

405
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,868
I can lose everything else, but not you.

406
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:47,537
You're mine, Ivy.

407
00:20:48,705 --> 00:20:50,249
You're mine. And, I'm yours.

408
00:20:51,541 --> 00:20:52,292
Okay?

409
00:20:57,422 --> 00:21:01,843
I guess our engagement party's
in full swing, then?

410
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:03,512
Yes.

411
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:08,100
But with some minor adjustments.

412
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:12,062
Like what exactly?

413
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:13,814
Nothing much.

414
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:17,067
I just want to make
our engagement party public.

415
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:19,945
You know people like love stories.

416
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:24,241
So, my plan is to hold
our engagement party

417
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:26,243
on the same day
as our campaign kick-off party.

418
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,664
Let's see if my ratings
don't go up after that.

419
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:38,171
Nice idea, Hon. You have my full support.

420
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:39,548
Thank you very much.

421
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:46,138
[suspenseful music playing]

422
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:54,062
[line ringing]

423
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:54,980
Hello?

424
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:59,901
Jaguar, I'm finally
in your lair. Where are you?

425
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:03,030
<i>Looks like someone's a little too excited.</i>

426
00:22:03,113 --> 00:22:05,240
<i>I can tell because you're in red tonight.</i>

427
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:10,203
So, where are you already?

428
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:12,539
I'm running out of patience, you know.

429
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:14,958
<i>All right, if that's what you want.</i>

430
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:17,210
<i>But before I reveal myself,</i>

431
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,671
<i>go through that door first.</i>

432
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:23,133
<i>I have a surprise waiting for you.</i>

433
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,559
Wow, Jaguar.

434
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:38,356
What if I fall for you
and you aren't ready?

435
00:22:40,150 --> 00:22:43,070
[slow tense music playing]

436
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:48,408
<i>There's your favorite wine.</i>

437
00:22:49,534 --> 00:22:50,535
<i>Help yourself.</i>

438
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:54,956
So… Where are you?

439
00:22:58,376 --> 00:23:01,379
<i>How about you turn around, Emilia?</i>

440
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:06,426
[suspenseful music playing]

441
00:23:14,142 --> 00:23:17,687
You truly are a sly being, Jaguar.

442
00:23:18,730 --> 00:23:21,024
I'm just being true to myself.

443
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:25,695
I'm just fast, agile, strong,

444
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:28,365
and, most of all, sly.

445
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:33,870
Well, if you really are fast,
strong, and sly, then,

446
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:36,039
why don't you come closer?

447
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:39,543
You Ardientes are so impatient.

448
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:42,504
We just met each other, Emilia.

449
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:45,757
You'll know my true nature soon enough.

450
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:46,800
But, first…

451
00:23:47,717 --> 00:23:51,471
I need to look into
the depths of your soul.

452
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:53,682
My soul?

453
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:54,933
Emilia…

454
00:23:55,809 --> 00:23:59,146
you should know
how obsessed I am with you.

455
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:04,985
That's why I saved you
from Natalie, remember?

456
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:06,903
Obsessed?

457
00:24:07,571 --> 00:24:09,489
I want to steal you away
from your husband.

458
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:12,701
I want to set you free.

459
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:17,330
And I want my love
to be the one to help you.

460
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:19,958
I'm already free, Jaguar.

461
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:21,168
[scoffs]

462
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:24,087
Let's not fool ourselves.

463
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:26,214
You aren't free.

464
00:24:27,090 --> 00:24:29,301
Until now, you're still being controlled.

465
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:34,556
By your father, your son,
and even by his fiancée.

466
00:24:34,639 --> 00:24:36,224
And, most especially,

467
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:38,685
by your beloved.

468
00:24:40,478 --> 00:24:42,731
But now, it's different.

469
00:24:43,231 --> 00:24:45,984
I'm here to change the rules of the game.

470
00:24:47,485 --> 00:24:49,529
I'll make you stronger.

471
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:51,573
I'll make all your dreams come true.

472
00:24:53,366 --> 00:24:59,831
And, I'll show you how it feels
to be worshipped, to be feared.

473
00:25:01,791 --> 00:25:04,127
I'll only believe you

474
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:08,048
if you come closer and show me your face.

475
00:25:08,131 --> 00:25:10,717
[suspenseful music playing]

476
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:12,636
Very well.

477
00:25:14,387 --> 00:25:15,388
Turn around then.

478
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:17,557
Okay.

479
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:21,728
I promise you that,

480
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:24,064
once you open your eyes,

481
00:25:24,439 --> 00:25:25,815
you'll finally know…

482
00:25:27,150 --> 00:25:30,070
the real Jaguar.

483
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:38,453
Go on, close your eyes.

484
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:42,624
[slow tense music playing]

485
00:26:41,433 --> 00:26:45,395
[tense piano music playing]

486
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:25,393
I'LL MAKE YOUR DREAMS COME TRUE.

487
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:27,145
BUT FIRST, HELP ME TAKE DOWN JULIO.

488
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:37,739
[pensive music playing]

489
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:46,206
Did that just really happen?

490
00:27:48,625 --> 00:27:49,501
[exhales sharply]

491
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:51,419
I can't believe this.

492
00:27:53,630 --> 00:27:55,548
Am I becoming an adulteress?

493
00:27:58,093 --> 00:28:00,387
Or am I becoming like Raul?

494
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:13,650
I'LL MAKE YOUR DREAMS COME TRUE.

495
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:14,901
BUT FIRST, HELP ME TAKE DOWN JULIO.

496
00:28:15,985 --> 00:28:18,530
[ominous music playing]

497
00:28:20,824 --> 00:28:23,076
The facts of the case show
the evidences against

498
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:24,911
my client are circumstantial.

499
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,663
He may have a witness,

500
00:28:26,746 --> 00:28:29,082
but there's nothing that
could corroborate his statement,

501
00:28:29,165 --> 00:28:31,042
so it's his word against my client's.

502
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:34,796
And I'm telling you, the witness
is perjuring himself.

503
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:37,132
With all due respect,

504
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:42,011
we all know why Diego is in prison.

505
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:44,639
That's because the judge

506
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,891
who used to handle this case
works for the Ardientes.

507
00:28:47,475 --> 00:28:49,978
I can understand your
frustration, Atty. Fisher.

508
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:50,895
And Miss Cruz,

509
00:28:50,979 --> 00:28:54,190
I've already reviewed the case
and found out that you're right.

510
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:58,111
Mr. Torillo is in prison
for a crime he didn't commit.

511
00:29:00,321 --> 00:29:03,408
Does that mean that Diego can go free?

512
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:04,576
It depends.

513
00:29:05,201 --> 00:29:07,787
If he agrees to my condition.

514
00:29:09,414 --> 00:29:10,623
What is it?

515
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:13,084
He should allow the Jaguar

516
00:29:13,168 --> 00:29:15,795
to be his backer and supporter
during the election.

517
00:29:16,212 --> 00:29:18,840
[tense music playing]

518
00:29:20,633 --> 00:29:25,972
I'd rather rot in prison
than become Jaguar's lapdog.

519
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:28,183
There's no law that states
I can't run for election

520
00:29:28,266 --> 00:29:30,059
while I'm in jail,

521
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:32,187
so we'll keep fighting.

522
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:34,439
Even though I'm in prison,

523
00:29:34,522 --> 00:29:36,441
I will still become a governor.

524
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:39,444
[Camia sighing]

525
00:29:39,527 --> 00:29:41,029
Diego, don't worry.

526
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:43,198
I'll take charge of the campaign.

527
00:29:43,990 --> 00:29:47,452
[somber music playing]

528
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:56,836
You're right that we can't
trust Jaguar so easily.

529
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:59,964
We don't know him
or just what he's capable of.

530
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:01,925
But Lily, what about Diego?

531
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:06,763
Mom, I'll find a way to help free Diego.

532
00:30:07,263 --> 00:30:12,685
But for now, I need to find out
who Jaguar is first.

533
00:30:14,187 --> 00:30:16,898
That way, before we meet with Judge Otico,

534
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:18,149
we'll know what to do.

535
00:30:19,234 --> 00:30:23,154
Diego will get out of prison
through legal means.

536
00:30:23,696 --> 00:30:26,199
[somber music continues playing]

537
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:28,660
Jaguar…

538
00:30:42,757 --> 00:30:43,716
Hmm…

539
00:30:44,592 --> 00:30:46,219
[singing]

540
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:48,221
[humming]

541
00:30:50,306 --> 00:30:52,308
It looks like you're having
a good day, Emilia.

542
00:30:54,352 --> 00:30:56,104
I heard you met with Jaguar.

543
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:58,648
What does he look like? Is he handsome?

544
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:00,233
[tense music playing]

545
00:31:00,316 --> 00:31:02,110
Honestly, I wouldn't know.

546
00:31:02,569 --> 00:31:04,779
He seems to be a mysterious man.

547
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:09,075
What did he say?

548
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,870
What did you talk about?

549
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,413
Did he offer help?

550
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:16,416
Not really.

551
00:31:16,499 --> 00:31:23,506
But I remember him saying that
he wants to steal me from you.

552
00:31:25,049 --> 00:31:26,092
He said that?

553
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:27,510
Mhm.

554
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:29,429
[scoffs]

555
00:31:29,804 --> 00:31:32,223
That bastard is out of his mind.

556
00:31:33,474 --> 00:31:34,726
He's insane.

557
00:31:35,768 --> 00:31:36,978
He said that?

558
00:31:37,061 --> 00:31:38,271
Are you jealous?

559
00:31:40,189 --> 00:31:42,525
Me? Jealous? Why would I be jealous?

560
00:31:43,943 --> 00:31:45,278
Huh? Why?

561
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:46,779
Will you leave me for him?

562
00:31:48,823 --> 00:31:50,783
I'm talking to you.
Are you going to leave me?

563
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:52,952
You won't, right?

564
00:31:53,453 --> 00:31:55,997
Besides, he's our family's enemy.

565
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:58,833
If your father finds out
you're making deals with him,

566
00:31:58,917 --> 00:32:00,585
you'll be in big trouble.

567
00:32:01,127 --> 00:32:03,755
Wait. How'd you find out about the deal?

568
00:32:04,088 --> 00:32:05,048
This.

569
00:32:06,591 --> 00:32:07,800
You left this lying around.

570
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:12,096
If your father finds out about
this, you know what will happen.

571
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:14,933
[tense music continues playing]

572
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:16,643
Be careful next time.

573
00:32:20,063 --> 00:32:21,981
Okay. I'll keep it.

574
00:32:23,107 --> 00:32:25,610
Emilia, Raul.

575
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:28,655
Julio wants to see us.

576
00:32:32,575 --> 00:32:35,286
What they're doing to Diego is too much!

577
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:36,496
That's right!

578
00:32:37,121 --> 00:32:38,790
Let's fight for Diego!

579
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:40,708
Let's organize a rally

580
00:32:40,792 --> 00:32:42,752
in front of the office
of those corrupt judges!

581
00:32:42,835 --> 00:32:45,463
[all] That's right! Let's hold a rally!

582
00:32:45,546 --> 00:32:47,173
Hold on! Wait!

583
00:32:48,508 --> 00:32:50,134
Please calm down!

584
00:32:50,510 --> 00:32:51,552
Calm down!

585
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:55,765
Diego said we shouldn't worry about him.

586
00:32:55,848 --> 00:32:59,727
We should just focus on our campaign.

587
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:03,356
Let's generate buzz for Diego.

588
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:06,609
And let's show those Ardientes

589
00:33:06,693 --> 00:33:08,319
that even though Diego's in prison

590
00:33:08,403 --> 00:33:12,240
and that they have control
over this entire province,

591
00:33:13,199 --> 00:33:17,120
we can beat them if we work together.

592
00:33:17,203 --> 00:33:19,247
-That's right, Ms. Camia.
-Friends.

593
00:33:19,330 --> 00:33:21,624
Let's do this for Diego!

594
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:22,959
[all] For Diego!

595
00:33:23,042 --> 00:33:25,044
For real change!

596
00:33:25,128 --> 00:33:27,255
[all] For real change!

597
00:33:27,338 --> 00:33:28,256
[applauding]

598
00:33:28,339 --> 00:33:30,049
-Diego!
-Diego!

599
00:33:30,758 --> 00:33:32,927
[tense music playing]

600
00:33:34,637 --> 00:33:38,057
You will all make
a public appearance tomorrow.

601
00:33:38,391 --> 00:33:42,562
That way, we could invite the public

602
00:33:42,937 --> 00:33:46,190
to the kick-off party
of Arnaldo's campaign.

603
00:33:46,649 --> 00:33:47,692
Yes, Grandpa.

604
00:33:47,775 --> 00:33:50,820
We will also invite them
to our engagement party.

605
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:52,739
The more they feel included,

606
00:33:52,822 --> 00:33:54,866
the more inclined
they'll be to support us.

607
00:33:55,658 --> 00:33:57,452
[slow tense music playing]

608
00:33:57,827 --> 00:33:58,953
[Julio] That's right.

609
00:33:59,037 --> 00:33:59,871
Now.

610
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:01,456
Reminder.

611
00:34:02,790 --> 00:34:03,541
Please.

612
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:07,086
I don't want another scandal tomorrow.

613
00:34:08,421 --> 00:34:10,006
Keep it friendly.

614
00:34:11,215 --> 00:34:13,926
I want everyone to smile
and be on their best behavior.

615
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:19,223
Especially you, Emilia.
Control your emotions.

616
00:34:19,932 --> 00:34:21,142
[mouthing]

617
00:34:32,445 --> 00:34:35,448
How are you guys doing?
You're running out of bags.

618
00:34:35,531 --> 00:34:38,159
Replenish them, okay? Thank you.

619
00:34:39,202 --> 00:34:40,578
[indistinct chatter]

620
00:34:40,661 --> 00:34:42,288
[Loring] Let's get more over there.

621
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:46,125
[Pandoy] But these are already divided.

622
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:48,002
It's great that it's here in town…

623
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:51,005
[tense music playing]

624
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:53,299
THE ARDIENTES WILL MAKE
A PUBLIC APPEARANCE TO INVITE

625
00:34:55,968 --> 00:34:56,844
[phone chimes]

626
00:34:58,096 --> 00:34:59,806
THE ARDIENTES WILL MAKE
A PUBLIC APPEARANCE TO INVITE

627
00:34:59,889 --> 00:35:01,349
THE PUBLIC TO ARNALDO'S
CAMPAIGN KICK-OFF PARTY.

628
00:35:01,432 --> 00:35:02,600
GENERATE BUZZ FOR DIEGO TOO.

629
00:35:06,395 --> 00:35:11,067
WE'RE READY FOR THE ARDIENTES.

630
00:35:13,986 --> 00:35:15,029
[phone buzzing]

631
00:35:16,030 --> 00:35:18,074
WE'RE READY FOR THE ARDIENTES.

632
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:26,999
Hello, everyone.

633
00:35:27,750 --> 00:35:28,835
Please have this.

634
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:31,170
I prepared something for you
so don't miss it, okay?

635
00:35:31,254 --> 00:35:33,089
-See you there!
-Tell the others too.

636
00:35:33,172 --> 00:35:35,716
Bring your friends, your families.

637
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:37,802
Everyone you want.

638
00:35:38,803 --> 00:35:40,930
-Oh, our enemies.
-Diego might be in jail,

639
00:35:41,013 --> 00:35:43,182
but he still won in the second survey.

640
00:35:43,266 --> 00:35:48,855
That means we are all sick
of the Ardientes.

641
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:53,568
Good grief, Camia.
What are you doing here?

642
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,862
The right thing, Emilia.

643
00:35:55,945 --> 00:36:01,159
You don't own Ardiente, so we
can campaign anywhere we want.

644
00:36:02,368 --> 00:36:03,119
[sighing]

645
00:36:03,911 --> 00:36:04,829
Let's go.

646
00:36:04,912 --> 00:36:07,081
Let's go and find another place.

647
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:07,915
Come on, everyone.

648
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:10,960
Good idea. You are so right, son.

649
00:36:11,043 --> 00:36:12,211
We should leave

650
00:36:12,295 --> 00:36:16,549
and look for a place
without trash lying around.

651
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,759
Emilia, you're the one who's garbage!

652
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:20,553
You are all trash!

653
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:24,182
You framed Diego,
you good-for-nothing cheaters!

654
00:36:24,765 --> 00:36:25,725
-[slapping]
-Shut up!

655
00:36:25,808 --> 00:36:27,226
-[slapping]
-You should shut up!

656
00:36:27,310 --> 00:36:28,060
Ms. Camia…

657
00:36:28,644 --> 00:36:30,313
Wait! You can't stop me.

658
00:36:30,396 --> 00:36:31,147
Hold this.

659
00:36:31,564 --> 00:36:33,107
-[tense music playing]
-[Marlon] Wait.

660
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:34,317
[Ivy] Emilia!

661
00:36:34,817 --> 00:36:36,360
Emilia, that's enough!

662
00:36:37,653 --> 00:36:38,404
Camia!

663
00:36:39,447 --> 00:36:40,615
-Stop them!
-That's enough!

664
00:36:40,698 --> 00:36:41,741
I told you to stop them!

665
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:43,659
That's enough!

666
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:44,744
Camia!

667
00:36:45,328 --> 00:36:46,913
You ruined my hair!

668
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:49,624
Is that all you got, Emilia?

669
00:36:49,707 --> 00:36:52,210
Or do you want me to shove
your face into the mud?!

670
00:36:52,293 --> 00:36:54,128
Why, do you miss the dirt, Camia?

671
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:55,171
Don't worry.

672
00:36:55,254 --> 00:36:58,424
I'll make sure you return
to the grave where you belong.

673
00:36:58,507 --> 00:37:02,303
So? You're confessing
in front of all these people

674
00:37:02,386 --> 00:37:04,472
that you had me buried alive!

675
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:06,265
I didn't say such a thing.

676
00:37:06,349 --> 00:37:08,476
A typical Ardiente!

677
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:11,896
You're great at making excuses
right after you slip up!

678
00:37:11,979 --> 00:37:13,648
But not anymore.

679
00:37:13,731 --> 00:37:16,609
You can't salvage
your tarnished reputation.

680
00:37:16,692 --> 00:37:20,780
Because I will see to it
that we will win this election!

681
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:23,658
[tense music playing]

682
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:26,244
-Don't be so sure.
-Bring them down!

683
00:37:26,327 --> 00:37:27,912
Bring them down! All of the Ardientes!

684
00:37:27,995 --> 00:37:29,622
-Let's go.
-Bring them down!

685
00:37:29,705 --> 00:37:32,291
Bring them down! All of the Ardientes!

686
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:35,336
Bring them down! All of the Ardientes!

687
00:37:39,173 --> 00:37:42,343
-I swear, that woman, Auntie?
-Emilia, are you okay?

688
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:45,888
I am going to do something
when I get my position back!

689
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:47,265
[Emilia grunting]

690
00:37:47,348 --> 00:37:50,309
I can't take it anymore.
I want to smack her in the face!

691
00:37:50,393 --> 00:37:51,769
Shut up, Emilia!

692
00:37:53,896 --> 00:37:56,399
Stop wagging your tongue!

693
00:37:57,441 --> 00:37:59,026
-You know--
-Is it my fault again?!

694
00:37:59,402 --> 00:38:04,198
You know, that had to happen,
so you can wake up to the truth.

695
00:38:04,782 --> 00:38:05,992
You're such an idiot!

696
00:38:06,075 --> 00:38:07,702
Do you know what you did earlier?

697
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:11,289
You showed the people
that you are unstable,

698
00:38:11,372 --> 00:38:13,582
that you are a psychotic woman!

699
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:15,876
Why are you blaming it on me again, Papa?!

700
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:19,380
-I was defending our family!
-You didn't defend anyone!

701
00:38:19,463 --> 00:38:21,757
You only brought more shame to our family!

702
00:38:21,841 --> 00:38:26,262
You women! You truly
are lesser beings than men!

703
00:38:26,804 --> 00:38:29,015
[tense music playing]

704
00:38:29,098 --> 00:38:32,935
Yeah right, Papa!
Well, you men are narrow-minded!

705
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:37,690
You can't just accept the fact
that our unpredictability

706
00:38:37,773 --> 00:38:38,607
makes you uneasy!

707
00:38:38,691 --> 00:38:41,110
Unpredictability, my ass!

708
00:38:42,194 --> 00:38:43,779
You and your stupid whims!

709
00:38:44,780 --> 00:38:46,907
You're the reason why our plans fail!

710
00:38:48,409 --> 00:38:52,371
It's better if you just shut up
and get out of my face

711
00:38:52,455 --> 00:38:54,790
before I break this on your head!

712
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:57,126
That's enough! You're going
to hurt somebody again!

713
00:38:57,209 --> 00:38:59,086
I can't let you hurt my wife!

714
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,172
I'll just hurt both of you then!

715
00:39:01,255 --> 00:39:02,465
-Why?
-You always do that!

716
00:39:02,548 --> 00:39:03,341
You always blame me!

717
00:39:03,424 --> 00:39:05,468
And now you want to hit me again, Papa?

718
00:39:05,551 --> 00:39:06,552
-Why?
-That's enough! Let's go!

719
00:39:06,635 --> 00:39:08,346
-Do you like being abused?!
-Why?

720
00:39:08,429 --> 00:39:09,680
Do you enjoy hurting people?!

721
00:39:09,764 --> 00:39:11,265
[Julio] Why? You're starting to like it?!

722
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:12,183
[Emilia] No!

723
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:15,436
You're starting to like being slapped!

724
00:39:16,103 --> 00:39:17,855
[tense music playing]

725
00:39:17,938 --> 00:39:18,814
This woman!

726
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:20,816
Julio.

727
00:39:21,275 --> 00:39:22,068
Congressman.

728
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,153
-Are you okay?
-Guard, guard!

729
00:39:24,236 --> 00:39:25,363
Water, please. Now.

730
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:26,947
Hon, is he okay?

731
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:28,866
Just relax? Just relax?

732
00:39:28,949 --> 00:39:29,784
-Water.
-I'm fine!

733
00:39:31,202 --> 00:39:32,745
Call a doctor! Now!

734
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:36,082
Oh!

735
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:42,171
If I were Ms. Camia, I would've
shoved Emilia's face in the mud!

736
00:39:42,254 --> 00:39:48,511
So she could experience all
our hardships under their rule!

737
00:39:49,136 --> 00:39:52,640
I'm thankful that they didn't
hurt Aunt Camia.

738
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:55,851
If they laid a hand on Ms. Camia,

739
00:39:55,935 --> 00:39:58,646
they'd taste the wrath of Team Diego!

740
00:39:59,063 --> 00:40:01,482
That's correct! I'll smack them good!

741
00:40:01,565 --> 00:40:05,444
[laughing]

742
00:40:06,946 --> 00:40:09,698
[pensive music playing]

743
00:40:09,782 --> 00:40:10,783
What is it, Diego?

744
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,327
I need to get out of here.

745
00:40:14,703 --> 00:40:17,123
I'm dragging Aunt Camia into my mess.

746
00:40:17,206 --> 00:40:19,500
This is my fight. I should be facing them!

747
00:40:19,959 --> 00:40:21,252
What are you going to do?

748
00:40:22,169 --> 00:40:24,588
Are you going to accept Jaguar's offer?

749
00:40:30,177 --> 00:40:31,804
Your dad keeps going too far, Emilia!

750
00:40:31,887 --> 00:40:34,181
Everything he's done
to make our lives miserable

751
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:36,392
will come back to him, mark my words.

752
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:39,228
You should just accept Jaguar's offer.

753
00:40:39,311 --> 00:40:41,147
[somber music playing]

754
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:43,315
If you're still hoping
that your dad will help you,

755
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:46,485
give you a position or power,
that's impossible, Emilia.

756
00:40:46,569 --> 00:40:48,279
Raul, can you just do me a favor?

757
00:40:48,362 --> 00:40:49,613
Can you get me a drink?

758
00:40:50,364 --> 00:40:52,992
I'm going to have a migraine,
a severe one.

759
00:41:02,751 --> 00:41:06,755
<i>That Jaguar guy is just</i>
<i>fooling you, Emilia.</i>

760
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:10,384
<i>Papa, that's why I need</i>
<i>to meet up with him</i>

761
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:13,137
<i>so I can turn the tables on him.</i>

762
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:14,472
<i>Well…</i>

763
00:41:14,722 --> 00:41:17,349
[ominous music playing]

764
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:20,603
<i>Should you get the chance…</i>

765
00:41:21,395 --> 00:41:23,772
<i>I want you to kill that fool,</i>

766
00:41:23,981 --> 00:41:26,275
<i>so I won't have any more problems.</i>

767
00:41:26,692 --> 00:41:27,526
<i>Okay, Papa.</i>

768
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:30,696
<i>I'll do exactly what you want me to do.</i>

769
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:32,698
<i>-Yes!</i>
<i>-But with some conditions.</i>

770
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:35,367
<i>Conditions?</i>

771
00:41:35,451 --> 00:41:36,285
<i>Yes, Papa.</i>

772
00:41:36,368 --> 00:41:39,079
<i>Now you're giving me conditions?</i>

773
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,207
[tense music playing]

774
00:41:42,541 --> 00:41:44,418
<i>Okay, just for the heck of it.</i>

775
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:46,504
<i>Come out with it.</i>

776
00:41:46,587 --> 00:41:49,256
<i>-What are your conditions?</i>
<i>-Okay.</i>

777
00:41:49,965 --> 00:41:53,260
<i>First, you'll forget all the mistakes</i>

778
00:41:53,344 --> 00:41:54,595
<i>I've made in the past.</i>

779
00:41:55,429 --> 00:41:56,222
<i>And of course,</i>

780
00:41:56,305 --> 00:41:58,807
<i>you'll also forgive me</i>
<i>for all my faults against you.</i>

781
00:41:59,350 --> 00:42:02,686
<i>And most importantly, you'll allow me</i>

782
00:42:02,770 --> 00:42:04,688
<i>to replace you in congress.</i>

783
00:42:06,899 --> 00:42:07,775
[laughing]

784
00:42:07,858 --> 00:42:09,944
<i>Take it or leave it.</i>

785
00:42:17,368 --> 00:42:21,247
<i>I'll take it. Why not? I'll take it.</i>

786
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:24,750
<i>But since you're a woman,</i>

787
00:42:25,709 --> 00:42:28,087
<i>I'm sure you're going to fail.</i>

788
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:31,382
<i>Not this time around, Papa.</i>

789
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:35,135
<i>I will not fail you</i>
<i>and I promise you that.</i>

790
00:42:35,511 --> 00:42:38,806
[ominous music continues]

791
00:42:43,978 --> 00:42:44,812
[sighs]

792
00:42:45,312 --> 00:42:47,690
-[phone buzzing]
-[suspenseful music playing]

793
00:42:47,773 --> 00:42:48,691
Hello.

794
00:42:53,696 --> 00:42:56,031
Tell them that Jaguar
is ready to meet with them.

795
00:43:01,745 --> 00:43:03,831
How are you, Mom? Are you hurt?

796
00:43:04,456 --> 00:43:07,001
Don't worry about me, Lily. I'm fine.

797
00:43:07,668 --> 00:43:09,753
I can't stop myself from worrying.

798
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,422
If it were up to me,

799
00:43:11,755 --> 00:43:14,592
I would forbid you
from facing off with Emilia.

800
00:43:14,675 --> 00:43:17,928
I'm scared that one day, she'll snap,

801
00:43:18,012 --> 00:43:19,388
grab a gun and…

802
00:43:20,806 --> 00:43:22,224
kill you.

803
00:43:23,058 --> 00:43:24,393
I'm sorry, Lily.

804
00:43:25,769 --> 00:43:27,730
I lost my cool.

805
00:43:27,813 --> 00:43:29,773
I got so infuriated and angry
with that woman.

806
00:43:30,774 --> 00:43:32,735
But I promise it won't happen again.

807
00:43:33,652 --> 00:43:34,987
Mom, I know it's hard.

808
00:43:35,738 --> 00:43:37,197
But as much as possible…

809
00:43:38,741 --> 00:43:40,951
as much as possible, please lie low.

810
00:43:44,913 --> 00:43:46,498
We need to talk about Diego.

811
00:43:47,833 --> 00:43:51,003
I figured that while
the Ardientes are down,

812
00:43:51,086 --> 00:43:55,090
now is the right time to free Diego.

813
00:43:55,174 --> 00:43:57,176
It's time to strengthen his campaign.

814
00:43:59,011 --> 00:44:00,763
Lily, it's going to be difficult.

815
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:05,851
Because Jaguar's meddling
with Diego's case.

816
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:09,229
He's another headache.

817
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:11,440
Okay.

818
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:13,400
I'll take care of it, Mom.

819
00:44:16,403 --> 00:44:17,780
Your father is right.

820
00:44:18,572 --> 00:44:21,283
You should've just ignored Camia.

821
00:44:21,784 --> 00:44:25,329
Come on, Auntie. Ivy beat me up.

822
00:44:25,412 --> 00:44:28,332
And then that Natalie kidnapped me

823
00:44:28,415 --> 00:44:32,086
and pretended to be Lily Cruz. And now…

824
00:44:32,169 --> 00:44:36,090
I just saw Camia, so I took out
all my anger on her.

825
00:44:36,757 --> 00:44:39,677
It looked like it was
the other way around.

826
00:44:40,302 --> 00:44:42,638
Stop mocking me, Auntie. Come on.

827
00:44:42,721 --> 00:44:43,931
I'll redeem myself.

828
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,140
Don't you worry.

829
00:44:46,141 --> 00:44:47,184
What's your plan?

830
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:51,772
Well, that's between me and Jaguar.

831
00:44:52,231 --> 00:44:54,024
[tense music playing]

832
00:44:54,108 --> 00:44:55,317
[knocking]

833
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:58,320
Ma'am, these are for you.

834
00:44:58,404 --> 00:44:59,571
What?

835
00:45:02,157 --> 00:45:04,368
Okay. What's this again?

836
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:06,495
Hmm…

837
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:08,872
Gifts.

838
00:45:11,417 --> 00:45:12,751
[chuckles]

839
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:15,712
Gifts, gifts, gifts. I love gifts.

840
00:45:17,089 --> 00:45:18,715
Stop worrying, Grandpa.

841
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:21,343
Okay? I will crush Diego's support group.

842
00:45:21,427 --> 00:45:24,930
And I promise you, I'll be epic
in that campaign kickoff.

843
00:45:25,931 --> 00:45:28,434
You better be and you should be.

844
00:45:28,934 --> 00:45:34,481
Because if you fail at your
own event, it'll be your end.

845
00:45:35,607 --> 00:45:37,067
That's not going to happen.

846
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:39,653
He can't do that and he never will.

847
00:45:39,736 --> 00:45:40,696
Okay?

848
00:45:40,779 --> 00:45:43,907
He can't even leave the prison
I put him in.

849
00:45:46,076 --> 00:45:48,745
I promise you, I will save our position.

850
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:50,456
I'll take care of our name.

851
00:45:51,373 --> 00:45:54,168
The name Ardiente will continue
to rule the people.

852
00:45:54,960 --> 00:45:56,712
[tense music playing]

853
00:46:00,674 --> 00:46:03,635
<i>Just accept Jaguar's help.</i>

854
00:46:03,719 --> 00:46:05,637
<i>I will accept your offer,</i>
<i>but on one condition.</i>

855
00:46:05,721 --> 00:46:09,057
<i>We have an invitation</i>
<i>from the rival party.</i>

856
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:12,019
<i>They said we shouldn't miss it.</i>

857
00:46:12,102 --> 00:46:16,690
[Arnaldo] <i>Let me introduce you</i>
<i>all to your future first lady.</i>

858
00:46:16,773 --> 00:46:18,400
-[cheering]
-[applauding]

859
00:46:18,484 --> 00:46:21,487
<i>Ivy Aguas, will you marry me?</i>

860
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:23,530
<i>-Yes. Yes!</i>
<i>-Yes!</i>

861
00:46:23,614 --> 00:46:25,616
<i>Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!</i>

862
00:46:25,699 --> 00:46:27,284
<i>Diego, Diego!</i>

863
00:46:27,367 --> 00:46:29,286
<i>-So!</i>
<i>-Diego, Diego!</i>

864
00:46:29,369 --> 00:46:30,996
[Diego] <i>Were you surprised?</i>

865
00:46:31,079 --> 00:46:33,373
<i>Yes, I'm a free man now!</i>

866
00:46:33,457 --> 00:46:36,627
[tense music playing]
